# Resend — server-side only. Never prefix these with VITE_.
#
# These are set in the Vercel project's Environment Variables, NOT in a local
# .env committed to git. The site's forms post to the serverless function at
# /api/send, and only that function reads them. Because none of these names
# carries a VITE_ or NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, Vite never inlines them into the
# browser bundle, so none of these values can leak to a visitor.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Resend account -> API Keys -> create a key.
#   2. Resend -> Domains -> add and verify healthyhome.com.np (or a subdomain
#      such as mail.healthyhome.com.np) by adding the DNS records Resend gives
#      you. Sending is rejected until the domain is verified, so skip this and
#      nothing will send.
#   3. Add the three variables below in Vercel -> Project -> Settings ->
#      Environment Variables, for Production (and Preview if you want to test).
#   4. Redeploy. Vercel only injects env vars at build/deploy time.

RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_TO_EMAIL=
RESEND_FROM=